# netsurf: fractional letter- and word-spacing (patch 227)
# Generated 2026-10-10
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser 114d6b0 (patch stack through 226)
#
# Fixes a shortfall in patch 220, which truncated letter-spacing and
# word-spacing to whole pixels per character: 0.1em at 16px added 1px a
# letter instead of 1.6 (+10 over ten letters, Chromium +16), 0.5px added
# nothing, and the error grew with the text.
#
#  - plot_style.h: PLOT_SPACING_SCALE (256); the two fields are in
#    1/PLOT_SPACING_SCALE px.
#  - html/font.c: resolved at that precision (css_fixed / 4).
#  - html/redraw.c: justification's per-space expansion (whole px) is
#    scaled to the same unit before it is added to word_spacing.
#  - vita/text.c, text.h: vita_text_advance_q() gives an advance in those
#    units; vita_text_width() sums them and rounds once (vita_text_px), and
#    the draw loop places each glyph at the rounded running sum, so drawn
#    and measured widths agree. vita_text_advance() rounds one advance.
#  - vita/layout.c: position and split accumulate the same units and round
#    as width does.
# With no spacing every advance is a whole number of pixels, so text is
# measured and placed exactly as before.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/CSS-fractional-spacing.html (FRACSP227, 4 checks,
# Chromium 4/4; with 220 alone, 1/4): 0.1em x 10 letters +16, 0.5px x 10
# +5, word-spacing 2.5px x 4 spaces +10, and a -0.31em letter-spacing
# grid of four 25% columns on one row (a guard: patch 226 already fixes
# that one). SPACING220 3/3 and the justified paragraph unchanged.
diff --git a/content/handlers/html/font.c b/content/handlers/html/font.c
